    "q-164274": {
      "dom_id": "step-q164274",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{25}=-1,$ find its $z$-intercepts.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the $z$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{4}+{0}^{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{25} & =-1 \\\\ 1-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{25} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{{z}^{2}}{25} & =-2 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =50 \\\\ z & =\\pm 5\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $z=-5\\sqrt{2}$ and $z=5\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $z$-axis are $(0,0,-5\\sqrt{2})$ and $(0,0,5\\sqrt{2}).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
