    "q-164232": {
      "dom_id": "step-q164232",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}=-1$, find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$",
      "worked_solution": "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1 & ={z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2} & =1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} \\\\ {z}^{2} & =\\pm \\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square root is defined only for non-negative arguments. However, notice that for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $z(x,y)$ is ${R}^{2}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
