    "q-164307": {
      "dom_id": "step-q164307",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet $(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-(z-3)^{2}=1,$ find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$",
      "worked_solution": "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-(z-3)^{2} & =1 \\\\ (x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-1 & =(z-3)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(z-3)^{2} & =(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-1 \\\\ z-3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-1} \\\\ z & =3\\pm \\sqrt{(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-1 & \\ge 0 \\\\ (x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2} & \\ge 1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the exterior of the circle $(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ which includes the boundary.\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1\\}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-164307-a",
