    "q-71957": {
      "dom_id": "step-q71957",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "What is the trace in the $xy$-plane of the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{6}=1?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the trace in the $xy$-plane, we substitute $z=0$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{6}=1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola in $xy$-plane.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
